    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36614" root="كت" body-key="k">
    
      R. Q. 1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَتْكَتَ</span></b> , inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَتْكَتَةٌ</span>, (in the K,
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَتْكَتٌ</span>, which is a mistake, TA,) <i>It</i> (a <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حُبَارَى</span>,
or bustard,) <i>uttered its cry.</i> (L, K, &amp;c.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2- 
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَتْكَتَ</span>, inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَتْكَتَةٌ</span>, (S, &amp;c.,) <i>He laughed
gently,</i> or <i>lowly:</i> (K:) <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كتكتة</span>, in laughing, is
less than <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَهْقَهَةٌ</span>: (S:) or like what is termed
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَنِينٌ</span>. (Th, El-Ahmar.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَتْكَتَ فِى ضَحِكِهِ</span>
<i>He laughed vehemently, immoderately,</i> or <i>excessively; i. q.</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَغْرَبَ</span>, q. v. (A.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A3-  See also 1.

